  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Bhuneshwar Sahu vs The State Of Jharkhand on 12 August, 2015 Author: D. N. Upadhyay Bench: D. N. Upadhyay In The High Court Of Jharkhand At Ranchi A. B. A. No.2347 of 2015 ----- Bhuneshwar Sahu. .......... Petitioner. -Versus- State of Jharkhand. .......... Opposite Party. ------ Coram : Hon'Ble Mr. Justice D. N. Upadhyay ------",
    "facts": "The petitioner is an accused in a case registered under Sections 3(zz)(iii) and (viii) of the F.S.S. Act, punishable under Section 59(iii) read with Sections 26 and 27 of Food Safety & Standard Act, 2006. The petitioner has been prosecuted for having been found in possession of adulterated food. It it is submitted that no injury has been caused to any one. Only on the basis of report submitted, complaint has been filed under Section 59(iii) of the Food Safety & Standard Act, 2006. Counsel for the State has opposed the petitioner's prayer for anticipatory bail.",
